      "writtenOn": "2023-02-20T18:12:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sometimes  We have to consider different aspect while exposing apis.\n\nI prefer to keep advertiser \u0026 scan filter implementation separately, because scan filter part were never symmetric with advertiser for other scan filters also. I have explained in details in other comments     \n \nAs per my opinion,  Multiple TransportDiscoveryData list should not be exposed to app for advertiser side or scanner side, beacuse TransportDiscoveryData can consist of multiple transportBlock, which is already solving same purpose. \n\none transport block represent one service, if particular app needs multiple services, which need to be advertised, the it should add those service as multiple Transport Block.\n\nSo one particular 3rd party APP/System APP should add one TransportDiscoveryData(it may have multiple block)  while starting advertisement for particular advertiser set, \n \nTDS spec: The structure of the Transport Block may be repeated in case there are multiple services (on the same or different transports) to advertise simultaneously. The structure may repeat as long as there is space available. These Transport Blocks may be from the same organization or from different organizations. As per spec,  transportData length in one Transportblock can be upto  239 bytes.\n0x00 Transport Data field not present (i.e., 0 octets in length)\n0x01 – 0xEF\n(Note 1) Number of Octets in Transport Data field",
      "parentUuid": "cab09e6e_280f24be",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 504,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 554,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "a9e8d334b215a0c46c510de3e6ddfa9f001ff3cb",
