      "writtenOn": "2023-02-20T18:12:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@Jack I completely agree with you, our API design should be futuristic \u0026 it should incorporate all aspect of BT specification.\n\nSo we tried to changed WIFI NAN  filtering to generic Transport discovery data with Transport data mask filter for other org id(0x01 , 03, any future org id) while up streaming this feature.   newer version controller may support Transport data mask \u0026 Transport data based filter for other org id, which is not currently present.\n\nBut Sometimes We have to also consider other aspects  .\n\n1. scan filters requirements are not symmetric with advertiser for any scan filters \nhttps://source.android.com/static/docs/core/connect/bluetooth/Android-5.0-Bluetooth-HCI-Reqs.pdf, because scan filter has introduced additional masks parameter  for eg service_uuid, service_data_uuid, Manufacturer data, etc.\n\nSimilar API can be found on both advertiser  \u0026 scan filter for similar features, It was never grouped into one class to keep it symmetric   between advertiser/scanner \nhttps://developer.android.com/reference/android/bluetooth/le/AdvertiseData#getManufacturerSpecificData()\nhttps://developer.android.com/reference/android/bluetooth/le/AdvertiseData#getServiceSolicitationUuids()\nhttps://developer.android.com/reference/android/bluetooth/le/AdvertiseData#getServiceUuids()\nhttps://developer.android.com/reference/android/bluetooth/le/AdvertiseData#getServiceData()\n\nhttps://developer.android.com/reference/android/bluetooth/le/ScanFilter#getManufacturerData()\nhttps://developer.android.com/reference/android/bluetooth/le/ScanFilter#getManufacturerDataMask()\nhttps://developer.android.com/reference/android/bluetooth/le/ScanFilter#getManufacturerId()\nhttps://developer.android.com/reference/android/bluetooth/le/ScanFilter#getServiceData()\nhttps://developer.android.com/reference/android/bluetooth/le/ScanFilter#getServiceDataMask()\nhttps://developer.android.com/reference/android/bluetooth/le/ScanFilter#getServiceDataUuid()\nhttps://developer.android.com/reference/android/bluetooth/le/ScanFilter#getServiceSolicitationUuid()\nhttps://developer.android.com/reference/android/bluetooth/le/ScanFilter#getServiceSolicitationUuidMask()\nhttps://developer.android.com/reference/android/bluetooth/le/ScanFilter#getServiceUuid()\nhttps://developer.android.com/reference/android/bluetooth/le/ScanFilter#getServiceUuidMask()\n\nOur TDD implementation is also similar to other google APCF . I think their were some reasons to keep it separate.\na. To reduce code complexity \nb.  Max Data lengths(eg. manufacturer data, service, TransportData) threshold may be  different for scan filter \u0026 advertiser . \neg. example of existing  scan filter.\nAssume that Manufacturer data/Service Data is around 240~ bytes as long as it fits into one advertisement packet.   \n\nSo on advertiser side max Data len for Manufacturer data/Service data can be consider as 240~ bytes.\nBut on scanner side, if we are keeping scan filter, then this length need to be divided by 2, 120~ byte should be manufacturer data \u0026 another 120~ bytes manufacturer data for manufacturer masks, because Controllers shall be able to accept HCI Command packets with up to 255 bytes of data excluding the HCI Command packet header.\n\n2.  Multiple transport discovery data should never be usecase from API perspective  , because multiple transport block within transport discovery data is already there.  other APCF APIs also  support filter for only single service data uuid or single serviceSolicitationUuid or single  service uuid or single AD type.   Even though multiple service data uuid/serviceSolicitationUuid/Manufactuerer data/etc are supported on advertiser side \n\nFor TDD filtering ,  Scanner APP never know that , how many Transport blocks are included by advertisers,So i think  Single Transport Blocks specific scan filtering is more aligned with google APCF spec perspective.  controller will still parse TDD adv packet with multiple block to find, if particular service is present  or not in any blocks.\n\n\n3. TDD Scan filter(In Transport transportdata max length 119 bytes along with transportdatamask length 119 bytes  \u0026 advertiser(transportdata max length 239 bytes) requirement can be different.\nBTW, I tried to understand the purpose  of setter/getter api for transport data length of https://developer.android.com/reference/android/bluetooth/le/TransportBlock#getTransportDataLength(), but i could not understand, why it was introduced, can we not get this length using https://developer.android.com/reference/android/bluetooth/le/TransportBlock#getTransportData() byte array length\n\n\nI made all api to system api, i still prefer to keep current set api in scan filter  to align with google scan filter implementation .",
